.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1105 AM PDT Sun Oct 25 2026

Another VFR day is on tap for the region, with satellite showing
only high clouds streaming over us. Tonight, the upper level trough
will continue to track across the PacNW while troughing extends
south. This will allow for onshore flow to take hold of much of the
region and perhaps interact with the marine layer. Right now the
most likely sites to see any marine layer action or stratus seem to
be around the San Francisco/San Mateo Peninsula  and around the
Monterey Bay. Though confidence is moderate, so opted to keep the
hint of lower clouds in the forecast rather than socking areas in.
Should we see low clouds develop, the timing is currently between 6Z-
15Z with clouds lifting or mixing out by the late morning.

Vicinity of SFO...Quiet conditions continue as high clouds stream
overhead. Winds are expected to become onshore later this
afternoon, peaking between 10-15 kt, before decreasing to less than
10 kt during the overnight hours. As mentioned above there is signal
for some lower clouds to move into the SFO region, right now models
generally keep it west of the terminal and closer to the coast. Kept
the hint of MVFR cigs in the TAF as a result, with clouds lifting to
VFR cigs by late morning. Tomorrow afternoon, a strong push of
onshore winds is forecast. This will be close to the end of the TAF
cycle where we could see 15 kt sustained winds gusts up to 20-25 kt
through the early evening. Moderate to high confidence in the
forecast.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR conditions and onshore winds are
forecast for this afternoon. Tonight, the signal for some weak
offshore or southerly flow before becoming more light and variable
tomorrow morning. Models also show the potential for some MVFR
cigs around the region but not fully socking us in. Opted to keep
the SCT mention of MVFR cigs and wait to see how the models trend.
It could be have a few hours of BKN to OVC MVFR cigs overnight,
with skies mixing out by mid to late morning. Moderate confidence
in the forecast.

