.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 939 AM PDT Sun Oct 25 2026

Gentle north to northwest breezes gradually become moderate to
fresh  early this week. Strong gusts increase across the southern
coastal waters near Point Sur and Monterey Bay by Monday
afternoon, with some isolated near gale force gusts possible.
Moderate seas of 4 to 5 ft are expected today for the offshore
waters, but will build to 6 to 8 ft seas Monday into Tuesday.
Slight seas of 2 to 3 ft hold today at the immediate coastline and
build to moderate 4 to 6 ft for Monday.

